From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pwm: mtk-disp: Drive the MT6789 PWM as the MT8183's

The MT6789 entry copied the commit-register variant (a commit at 0xC), but
on the Minimal Phone MP01 the period and high width written that way never
reach the output: the controller reports 25% programmed (CON1 0x010003ff)
while GPIO84's pad, sampled 3000 times, never reads high. Setting
BLS_DEBUG (0x80) bits 0-1 makes the output follow the registers (pad
sampled at 12.7%, 26% and 79.7% for 12.5%, 25% and 78% programmed), which
is the MT8183 layout: CON0 0x18, CON1 0x1c and no commit register.

Use the MT8183 data for MT6789.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pwm/pwm-mtk-disp.c | 12 +-----------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pwm/pwm-mtk-disp.c b/drivers/pwm/pwm-mtk-disp.c
--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-mtk-disp.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-mtk-disp.c
@@ -274,16 +274,6 @@
 	.bls_debug_mask = 0x3,
 };
 
-static const struct mtk_pwm_data mt6789_pwm_data = {
-	.enable_mask = BIT(0),
-	.con0 = 0x18,
-	.con0_sel = 0x0,
-	.con1 = 0x1C,
-	.has_commit = true,
-	.commit = 0xC,
-	.commit_mask = 0x1,
-};
-
 static const struct mtk_pwm_data mt8173_pwm_data = {
 	.enable_mask = BIT(0),
 	.con0 = 0x10,
@@ -307,7 +297,7 @@
 static const struct of_device_id mtk_disp_pwm_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt2701-disp-pwm", .data = &mt2701_pwm_data},
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6595-disp-pwm", .data = &mt8173_pwm_data},
-	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6789-disp-pwm", .data = &mt6789_pwm_data},
+	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6789-disp-pwm", .data = &mt8183_pwm_data},
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8173-disp-pwm", .data = &mt8173_pwm_data},
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8183-disp-pwm", .data = &mt8183_pwm_data},
 	{ }
